cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "polyglot-code-guard"
# Keep `version` in lockstep with pyproject.toml [project].version and
# src/polyguard/__init__.py.
version: 0.5.0
authors:
  - name: "Furox-Art"
    email: "furkanarkn1451@gmail.com"
abstract: >-
  Fail-closed, multi-language test verification for AI-generated code.
  Polyguard discovers supported project types, checks for a test suite, runs the relevant
  build and test commands, and returns a one-word verdict by default. A passing exit code is
  not sufficient: a positive test-success summary from a recognized runner output format is
  also required after every discovered package.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Furox-Art/polyglot-code-guard"
url: "https://github.com/Furox-Art/polyglot-code-guard"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
keywords:
  - "testing"
  - "code-verification"
  - "polyglot"
  - "ai-generated-code"
  - "quality-gate"
